 oils, no artificial colors, flavors or sweeteners."}, {"type": "header", "content": "Point 3"}, {"type": "text", "id": "pot_i3_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "The dose"}, {"type": "text", "id": "pot_i3_title", "label": "Title", "default": "Full doses, tested"}, {"type": "textarea", "id": "pot_i3_text", "label": "Text", "default": "Every active at the dose used in human research, printed on the label and tested in the finished product."}, {"type": "header", "content": "Footnote"}, {"type": "textarea", "id": "pot_why", "label": "Why it matters", "default": "In a 2023 JAMA study, 22 of 25 melatonin gummies didn’t match their label, with actual doses from 74% to 347% of the amount stated. In 2024, NOW tested 12 creatine gummy brands and 6 failed to meet their label claim."}, {"type": "text", "id": "pot_source", "label": "Source", "default": "Cohen et al., JAMA, 2023; NOW, February 2024."}], "presets": [{"name": "Potency"}]}{% endschema %}
